    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The point of this entry is the status pair, not the theorem. `epistemic_status: open` says axeyum has not established it; `external_status: proved` says mathematics has. Before the second field, this fact was unwritable: `proved` would have claimed our kernel checked Wiles, `open` would have implied the question is unsettled, and `conjectured` would have been false since 1995.\n\nIt also marks a real boundary rather than a bookkeeping one. `formal.fragment` is `none`: nothing in this system decides it, and `pow` with a variable exponent is outside every fragment we implement. The statement is recorded in SMT-LIB shape anyway so the gap is legible and greppable -- an honest `none` is more useful than an omission, because it can be counted.\n\nThe self-extension loop must filter on `epistemic_status == open AND external_status != proved`, or it will spend its queue re-deriving the settled literature.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
